vdr-plugin-image-next: Debian/Ubuntu packaging
================================================

The original ffmpeg-free/MPEG-2 encoder warning in this file (2008) is
obsolete. The fork can render directly through VDR's true-colour OSD,
and keeps MPEG-2 still-image output as a compatibility fallback.

Runtime modes:
  Automatic (default)    - prefer native 32-bpp VDR OSD, else MPEG-2
  True-color OSD         - request native OSD, fallback when unavailable
  Legacy MPEG-2         - explicitly use old still-image device output

The Skindesigner API is an optional compile-time dependency. The build
uses pkg-config when libskindesignerapi is present; it also builds without
that library. Do not add a hard dependency on libskindesignerapi-dev for
platforms that do not ship it.

Skindesigner view template
--------------------------
The package installs:

  /usr/share/vdr-plugin-image-next/skindesigner/plug-image_next-grid.xml

Skindesigner templates are skin-specific. This file MUST be placed into
the xmlfiles/ directory of the ACTIVE Skindesigner skin, using the skin's
own installation mechanism, and the skin must be reloaded. The package
does not silently modify installed third-party skins. Native grid remains
available if the XML view is absent. The plugin's own README explains
the expected template name and native fallback.

The package never installs sample image sources automatically, does not
alter the user's photographs, and does not modify VDR's existing output
plugin configuration.
